cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "noisy-tv-instrumentation: measurement-noise capture in the intrinsic-motivation instrumentation of LLM agents"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for the article "Noisy-TV em agentes LLM" (Ulisses Flores, 2026).
  Minimal, execution-verified demonstrations of the cosine noise floor of embeddings
  (sigma ~= 0.177 at d=32, ~= 0.051 at d=384, ~ 1/sqrt(d)) and of the ghost-gap effect:
  a Goldilocks curiosity trigger (4*g*(1-g)) fed by that noise floor reads 0.58 of maximum
  intensity on an agent with literally nothing left to learn. Includes the measured data
  from the calibration of a real autonomous agent (daimon, private) and the bibliography
  connecting two literatures — the classic noisy-TV line in RL and the LLM-agent
  intrinsic-motivation instrumentation line — that do not cite each other.
